Elena: Quick docs snag /projects/{project_id} examples are inconsistent. Some examples use numeric IDs (1234), others use short slugs (my-proj) and some SDK snippets expect UUIDs like '8a1f4d6e-...'. Backend canonical id is UUID. The slug is an alias and numeric ids are legacy internal IDs. We need to standardize examples to UUIDs and add migration guidance.

Marcus: Oh wow. I saw the Rust SDK example that deserializes project.id into i64. That's definitely wrong. We need examples to show `id: string` and demonstrate UUID usage.

Elena: Agreed. Plan: 1) Update OpenAPI example values to use UUID v4 as primary example and mention slug/legacy numeric as secondary. 2) Update TypeScript/Rust/Go snippets to show id as string. 3) Add a tiny migration snippet showing how to resolve a slug to a UUID via lookup endpoint. 4) Add docs-e2e rule asserting examples for project_id match UUID regex.

Rory: I'll take the OpenAPI + SDK snippet changes. For the migration helper I'll add a TS snippet like this:```ts
// map slug/legacy id -> canonical uuid
async function resolveProjectId(client, maybeId: string|number) {
  if (typeof maybeId === 'number') {
    // legacy numeric id: call lookup endpoint that maps legacy ids to uuids
    const resp = await client.get(`/internal/ids/lookup?legacy=${maybeId}`)
    return resp.data.uuid
  }
  if (typeof maybeId === 'string' && /^[0-9a-fA-F-]{36}$/.test(maybeId)) {
    return maybeId // already uuid
  }
  // assume slug -> resolve via public lookup endpoint
  const r = await client.get(`/projects/by-slug/${encodeURIComponent(maybeId)}`)
  return r.data.id // canonical uuid
}
```

Marcus: Nice. For Rust I'll include a small note showing ProjectId = String in examples and a short helper to normalize values (parse integers -> call lookup, slugs -> call slug route). Don't change generated types yet  only examples and docs.

Elena: Also add an explicit sentence in the API reference: "project_id may be provided as a legacy numeric id or a short slug; however, all API responses and canonical identifiers are UUIDs. SDK examples use the canonical UUID string."

Rory: I'll open a draft PR that updates the OpenAPI examples, all SDK snippet files in examples/, and a new docs-e2e lint that scans example values for the project_id param and asserts they match the UUID v4 regex: `^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[1-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[89ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$` (case-insensitive).

docs-bot: Created issue #2475 and draft PR #3399: https://git.redwood/g/infra/docs/pulls/3399 (OpenAPI example updates, SDK snippet fixes, migration helper snippets, docs-e2e lint).

Marcus: I'll review the PR once it's up. One more ask: add a short regression test that parses the generated HTML for the endpoint and asserts the visible example contains a 36-char UUID (helps catch formatting issues where uuid gets truncated).

Rory: Good idea  adding that to the test plan. ETA for PR: tomorrow morning.

Elena: Thanks team. After merge I'll include a short line in the release notes and update the migration guide with the slug->uuid mapping steps.
